---
import '../styles/global.css';

const title = 'Privacy — MindLynx';
const updated = '27 July 2026';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-GB">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content="How MindLynx handles the details you send us." />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#07110f" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://mindlynx.ai/privacy" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="site-header is-scrolled">
      <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="MindLynx — home">
        <img class="brand-mark" src="/images/brand-mark.png" alt="" width="31" height="31" />
        MindLynx
      </a>
      <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Site">
        <a class="nav-cta" href="/#talk">Talk to us</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="legal">
      <div class="shell">
        <p class="section-label">Privacy</p>
        <h1>What we do with your details.</h1>
        <p class="legal-lead">
          Short version: we use what you send us to reply to you, and for the Albion waitlist if
          you ask for it. We don't sell it, share it, or add you to anything you didn't choose.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          Only what you type into the contact form: your name, your email address, what you're
          writing about, and your message. Nothing more. We don't use analytics, advertising
          trackers or third-party cookies on this site.
        </p>

        <h2>Why we hold it</h2>
        <p>
          To answer you. That's our legitimate interest in responding to someone who has
          deliberately contacted us. If you select <em>The Albion waitlist</em>, we also add your
          name and email to our Albion announcement list — that part is your consent, given by
          choosing it, and you can withdraw it whenever you like.
        </p>

        <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
        <p>
          Our email is delivered by <a href="https://resend.com/legal/dpa" rel="noopener">Resend</a>,
          which processes messages on our behalf and hosts the Albion list. The site is served by
          Render. Both act as processors under our instructions. Nobody else receives your details,
          and we never sell them.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Correspondence stays in our inbox while it's useful, and we clear it out when it isn't —
          within two years at the latest. Waitlist entries stay until Albion launches or until you
          unsubscribe, whichever comes first.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under UK GDPR you can ask us for a copy of what we hold, ask us to correct or delete it,
          object to how we're using it, or withdraw consent for the waitlist. Email
          <a href="mailto:hello@mindlynx.ai">hello@mindlynx.ai</a> and we'll action it — no forms,
          no friction. If we get it wrong, you can complain to the
          <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">Information Commissioner's Office</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          MindLynx Ltd, London, United Kingdom. Data protection questions go to
          <a href="mailto:hello@mindlynx.ai">hello@mindlynx.ai</a>.
        </p>

        <p class="legal-meta">Last updated {updated}.</p>
        <a class="partner-link" href="/">Back to MindLynx <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer class="site-footer">
      <div class="shell">
        <span>MindLynx Ltd · London</span>
        <span>Building in Britain · Building in the open</span>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
